    <bpmn:process id="W_W1221" name="W1221. Store-Level Typhoon Preparation, Merchandise Protection &amp; Quick Response Protocol" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: PAGASA raises Public Storm Warning Signal (PSWS) #1 or higher for province where BuildRight store is located; or 48 hours before projected typhoon landfall in any operating region
Frequency: ~8–12 typhoon warning activations per year affecting various regions; each store activates 2–4 times per year on average
Volume: 50–150 stores may be simultaneously in a typhoon&#x27;s path per major event
Owner: Regional Manager
Participants: Regional Manager, Store Manager, all store staff, COO, LP Officer, Facilities Maintenance, VP Supply Chain
Source: workflow W1221 — Store-Level Typhoon Preparation, Merchandise Protection &amp; Quick Response Protocol</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1221_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1221_Lane1" name="Regional Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1221_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1221_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1221_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1221_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1221_Lane2" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1221_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1221_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1221_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1221_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1221_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1221_Lane3" name="VP Supply Chain">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1221_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1221_End15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1221_Start5" name="PAGASA raises Public Storm Warning Signal (PSWS) #1 or higher for province where…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1221_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1221_Task6" name="T-48 hours (Signal #1 raised)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: T-48 hours (Signal #1 raised): Regional Manager activates Typhoon Preparation Protocol for affected stores: (a) sends automated notification to all Store Managers in affected provinces via SMS and store operations app, (b) cancels all non-essential deliveries to affected stores (reschedule DC replenishment), (c) instructs DC to hold outbound shipments for affected region, (d) Regional Manager establishes communication cadence: Store Managers report status every 6 hours
Responsible (R): Regional Manager
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 1 hour</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1221_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1221_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1221_Task7" name="T-24 hours">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: T-24 hours: Store Manager executes Tier 1 preparations: (a) outdoor lumber yard: strap down lumber stacks, move small items indoors, secure loose materials (tarps, nets, sandbags around cement stacks), (b) check roof drainage channels and clear debris, (c) reinforce store entrance and receiving dock doors with storm shutters or plywood, (d) test emergency generator: confirm fuel level ≥ 75%, test auto-start function per W913, (e) verify emergency supplies: flashlight, first aid kit, battery-powered radio, drinking water (3 days supply for staff who may shelter), (f) move highest-value portable merchandise (power tools, small appliances) from perimeter walls to interior displays
Responsible (R): Store Manager / All Staff
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: 4–6 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1221_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1221_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1221_Task8" name="T-12 hours (Signal #2 raised)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: T-12 hours (Signal #2 raised): Store Manager executes Tier 2 preparations: (a) move all floor-level merchandise to upper shelves or pallets (minimum 30cm elevation), (b) cover electrical and appliance displays with plastic sheeting, (c) secure outdoor signage — remove or bolt down banner stands and A-frame signs, (d) back up POS data and ensure offline capability per W535, (e) prepare store for early closure: complete all pending customer transactions, (f) Store Manager announces early closure time to staff and posts closure notice on store entrance and social media
Responsible (R): Store Manager / All Staff
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: 3–4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1221_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1221_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1221_Task9" name="T-0 (Signal #3 or #4 / landfall)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: T-0 (Signal #3 or #4 / landfall): (a) Store Manager closes store; secures all entry points; sets alarm; (b) staff dismissed with instruction to shelter at home or designated evacuation center; (c) minimum skeleton crew (Store Manager + 1 Maintenance) remains if store designated as community shelter by LGU — otherwise all staff evacuated, (d) system switches affected stores to &quot;Typhoon Closure&quot; mode: ecommerce platform shows &quot;temporarily closed&quot; for affected store pickup locations, BOPIS orders rerouted or suspended
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: 1–2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1221_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1221_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1221_Task10" name="During typhoon">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: During typhoon: Regional Manager maintains contact with Store Managers via battery-powered group chat (Viber/WhatsApp); Store Managers report: (a) staff safety status, (b) structural damage observed (if safe to assess), (c) flooding status; COO monitors overall situation and coordinates with VP Supply Chain on DC operations
Responsible (R): Regional Manager / Store Managers
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1221_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1221_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1221_Task11" name="Post-typhoon (T+6 to T+24 hours)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Post-typhoon (T+6 to T+24 hours): Once PAGASA downgrades signal and local government declares area safe: Store Manager conducts rapid damage assessment: (a) exterior: roof damage, signage damage, structural damage, flooding around store perimeter, (b) interior: water ingress, ceiling leaks, merchandise damage, equipment damage, (c) yard: lumber stack status, outdoor materials damage, (d) utilities: power status, water status, telecom status; Store Manager photographs all damage and submits Rapid Assessment Report via store operations app
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: 2–4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1221_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1221_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1221_Task12" name="Green">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Regional Manager reviews all Rapid Assessment Reports from affected region; categorizes stores: (a) Green (no significant damage) — authorize reopening within 24 hours, (b) Yellow (minor damage, safe to operate) — authorize reopening after minor repairs (1–3 days), (c) Red (major damage, unsafe) — store remains closed; Facilities Maintenance dispatched for emergency repairs; store staff temporarily redeployed to nearest open store
Responsible (R): Regional Manager
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 2–4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1221_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1221_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1221_Task13" name="Store reopening">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Store reopening: Store Manager conducts pre-opening safety check: (a) verify electrical system safe (no water in outlets/panels), (b) verify structural integrity (no compromised roof/walls), (c) clean and dry all affected surfaces, (d) restock damaged or displaced merchandise, (e) update ecommerce platform: store available for BOPIS, (f) post reopening announcement on social media; Store Manager confirms &quot;Open&quot; status in system
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: 4–8 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1221_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1221_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1221_Task14" name="Post-typhoon supply chain recovery">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: Post-typhoon supply chain recovery: (a) DC resumes operations if in affected region — assesses DC damage per parallel protocol, (b) Supply Planning re-routes replenishment from unaffected DCs to affected stores, (c) Logistics Coordinator re-establishes delivery routes (may require alternate routes due to road damage), (d) Merchandising prioritizes emergency replenishment of essential items (construction materials for community rebuilding, tarps, generators, water tanks — high post-typhoon demand)
Responsible (R): VP Supply Chain / Logistics Manager
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 3–7 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1221_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1221_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1221_End15" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1221_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1221_Annotation16">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-320 (ensure controlled execution — Crisis Response &amp; Recovery (PA-26.2).) | - operational: Regional Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Regional Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
