    <bpmn:process id="W_W1552" name="W1552. Typhoon Post-Event Rapid Store Damage Assessment, Safety Clearance &amp; Phased Reopening Protocol" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Typhoon Signal No. 2+ lifted in store&#x27;s area; or flood water receded from store vicinity; or earthquake &gt; Intensity V
Frequency: ~20–30 events/year affecting ~5–50 stores per event (Philippine typhoon belt)
Volume: Peak typhoon season (June–December) may have 2–3 events/month
Owner: Regional Manager
Participants: Regional Manager, Store Manager, Maintenance/Utility, COO, Facilities Manager, Safety Officer
Source: workflow W1552 — Typhoon Post-Event Rapid Store Damage Assessment, Safety Clearance &amp; Phased Reopening Protocol</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1552_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1552_Lane1" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1552_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1552_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1552_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1552_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1552_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1552_Lane2" name="Regional Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1552_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1552_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1552_Lane3" name="COO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1552_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1552_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1552_Start5" name="Typhoon Signal No. 2+ lifted in store&#x27;s area; or flood water receded from store vicinity…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1552_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1552_Task6" name="Initial safety check-in">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Initial safety check-in: Once storm signal is lifted, Store Manager conducts remote check-in — calls/texts store to verify Store Manager and staff safety; assesses personal situation (housing, family safety, transport availability); confirms ability to reach store within 4 hours; reports status to Regional Manager via emergency communication channel
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1552_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1552_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1552_Task7" name="Physical site assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Physical site assessment: Store Manager (or designated alternate) conducts physical assessment of store — uses standardized damage assessment checklist: (a) structural integrity (roof, walls, foundation, signs), (b) flooding (standing water level, water line mark, drainage status), (c) electrical system (power availability, wiring damage, panel condition), (d) inventory exposure (wet/damaged stock, lumber yard condition), (e) exterior (parking lot debris, fencing, loading bay); takes geo-tagged photos of each area; submits via mobile app
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: 1–2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1552_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1552_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1552_Task8" name="Safety classification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Safety classification: Regional Manager reviews assessment and classifies store: (a) Green — minor/no damage, safe to reopen immediately; (b) Amber — moderate damage, can open with restrictions (partial floor, limited hours, generator power); (c) Red — significant structural/flooding damage, unsafe to occupy until professional inspection and remediation
Responsible (R): Regional Manager
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 15 min/store</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1552_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1552_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1552_Task9" name="Green store rapid reopening">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Green store rapid reopening: For Green stores — Store Manager calls in available staff (may use skeleton crew if some employees are personally affected); restores systems (POS startup, network check, inventory spot check of high-value items); opens with reduced hours initially; prioritizes selling essential recovery materials (tarpaulins, plywood, CGI sheets, nails, tools)
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: 2–3 hours to reopen</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1552_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1552_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1552_Task10" name="Amber store restricted operations">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Amber store restricted operations: For Amber stores — Store Manager identifies safe zones within the store; closes off damaged/flooded areas; activates generator if grid power unavailable (W470); opens safe zones for limited operations; Maintenance/Utility begins cleanup of affected areas; Facilities Manager dispatches repair team for non-structural fixes
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Facilities Manager
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: 4–8 hours to partial reopen</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1552_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1552_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1552_Task11" name="Red store closure management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Red store closure management: For Red stores — Regional Manager confirms closure to COO; Facilities Manager dispatches structural engineer for professional assessment; Maintenance/Utility secures building (board-up, tarp) to prevent further damage; inventory salvage team deployed for recoverable merchandise (W91); insurance claim initiated (W59); HR coordinates employee temporary reassignment to nearby stores
Responsible (R): Regional Manager / Facilities Manager
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 1–2 days to secure site</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1552_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1552_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1552_Task12" name="Post-event reporting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Post-event reporting: COO compiles post-event report within 72 hours — stores affected by status (Green/Amber/Red), estimated revenue impact, estimated inventory loss, estimated repair cost, employee safety status, community relief contribution (W428); feeds into insurance claims and BCP improvement (W158)
Responsible (R): COO
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: 4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1552_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1552_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1552_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1552_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1552_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-320 (ensure controlled execution — Crisis Response &amp; Recovery (PA-26.2).) | - operational: Regional Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Regional Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
